+A 19-language override layer for DSH i18n (ja/ko/fr/...), migrated onto the
+native language-pack API of dsh 0.1.2-alpha.2: the browser half registers each
+third language with `ctx.locale.addLanguage({ id, label, fallback: 'en' })` and
+each namespace dictionary with `ctx.locale.register(ns, locale, dict)`. The
+languages appear in DSH's own Settings → General **Language** row alongside
+中文 / English, and the selection persists in the host-backed
+`locale.preference` setting instead of browser localStorage. Client-only
+plugin — the host half is a no-op stub.
+
+The 0.1.1-era mechanisms are retired: the `LocaleRuntime.prototype.lookup`
+monkey patch (its private signature became `(ns, key, chain)`, which the old
+two-argument wrapper could not carry), the custom
+`settings.general.item` "Language override" row, the
+`dsh-plugin-better-locale:active` localStorage store, and the private
+`ctx.betterLocale` service. DSH's own Language row, `locale.preference`
+setting, and `ctx.locale` service are the same entry points.
 
 Release procedure (internal):
 
